course: dictionary
lesson: 5529
title: Led: one word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: The word «led» is the past tense of «lead». It has many meanings, so the context tells you which one you need. «She led us to the park» means she showed the way by going in front. «He led a happy life» means he lived in a certain way. Put your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: Context also tells you when a word is a different word that looks the same. «An LED bulb makes light from tiny crystals.» Here LED is written in capitals and it means light-emitting diode, a kind of small light. It is not the past of lead. Capitals and the words around it are your clues.
explain: Sport and maths use led too. «Our team led by 2 goals at half time» means they were winning. In maths, a team that led by 3 points was 3 points ahead. Phrases like «led to», meaning caused, and «be led astray», meaning taken off the right path, are easiest to learn as whole chunks.
fact: «Led» is the past tense of «lead»: lead, leads, led, leading.
fact: «Led» can mean showed the way, was in charge, was winning, caused something, went in a direction, or lived a certain kind of life.
fact: «The path led to the river» means the path went in the direction of the river.
fact: «LED» in capitals is a different word: it stands for light-emitting diode.
fact: An LED bulb gives the same light as an old bulb for a fraction of the electricity, and it lasts years longer.
exercise: «The path led to the river.» What does led mean here? | Lived a happy life | Was in charge of a group | *Went in a certain direction | Was winning
exercise: «Many street lights are now LEDs.» What does LED stand for? | A metal used in old pipes | *Light-emitting diode, a small kind of light | Something that is winning | The past of lead
exercise: «Our team led by 2 goals at half time.» What does led mean here? | Caused a problem | Lived in an old house | Showed the way to the park | *Was winning
test: «She led us to the park.» What does led mean? | Was in charge of a team | *Showed the way by going in front | Was winning | Caused a noise
test: «The bad choice led to trouble.» What does led to mean? | Lived a happy life | Went in a certain direction | *Caused something to happen | Was in first place
exam: «An LED bulb uses little power.» What does LED stand for? | *Light-emitting diode | Lots of electricity | The past of lead | Lead, the heavy metal
